        // level down — RECURSE, so the `synthRetAnnots` pin fires for a lambda whose
        // NESTED literal field adopted a union-field shape (`objLitWidenFields`'
        // descent; without the pin its `$fnsig` kept the self-inferred plain layout —
        // INVALID-WASM, fuzz-nightly run 29808029476 seed 78530533 d5). A nested map
        // (`{[`) declines inside the recursion's own gate.
        //
        // The endpoint pre-filter this guard spelled out is DELETED rather than routed to
        // `nameIsBraceSpanEnds`: it was REDUNDANT. The recursion's own first line is
        // `canonBareShapeName(ftype)`, whose first two tests are `length < 2` and the same
        // `{`/`}` endpoint pair, so the call already answers `false` on exactly the names the
        // guard was rejecting. Both functions are pure, so removing it changes no answer and
        // costs one call on a field type that is about to be rejected by three compares.
        if nameIsStructWithUnionField(ftype) { return true }
      }
    }
    fi = fi + 1
  }
